@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam ArrowFontStyle plain
title Commenting on a student

box Logic LOGIC_COLOR_T1
participant ":LogicManager" as LogicManager LOGIC_COLOR
participant ":CommentCommandParser" as Parser LOGIC_COLOR
participant "c:CommentCommand" as CommentCommand LOGIC_COLOR
end box

box Model MODEL_COLOR_T1
participant "m:Model" as Model MODEL_COLOR
participant "p:Person" as Person MODEL_COLOR
participant "existing:Comment" as Existing MODEL_COLOR
end box

[-> LogicManager : execute("comment 3 c/asks good questions")
activate LogicManager

LogicManager -> Parser : parse("3 c/asks good questions")
activate Parser

note right of Parser
  AddressBookParser dispatches on the command word and is
  omitted. Rejected here with a ParseException: an index that
  is not a positive number, both comment prefixes at once,
  neither of them, or c/ with no text to add.
end note

Parser -> Parser : ParserUtil.parseComment(text)
activate Parser
note right of Parser
  Comment.isValidComment rejects text longer than MAX_LENGTH
  or holding control characters, so the comment c carries is
  already within the limit. An empty c-/ becomes Comment.EMPTY,
  which is the clear.
end note
Parser --> Parser : comment
deactivate Parser

Parser --> LogicManager : c
deactivate Parser

LogicManager -> CommentCommand : execute(m)
activate CommentCommand

CommentCommand -> Model : getFilteredPersonList()
activate Model
Model --> CommentCommand : lastShownList
deactivate Model

note right of CommentCommand
  Rejected with a CommandException before anything changes:
  an index past the end of the displayed list, and c-/ on its
  own when the student has no comment to clear.
end note

alt isReplacing, from c-/
  note right of CommentCommand
    The comment is used as it stands. Its length was
    settled when it was parsed, so nothing can push a
    replacement over the limit.
  end note

else appending, from c/
  CommentCommand -> Person : getComment()
  activate Person
  Person --> CommentCommand : existing
  deactivate Person

  CommentCommand -> Existing : lengthAfterAppending(comment)
  activate Existing
  Existing --> CommentCommand : combinedLength
  deactivate Existing

  opt combinedLength > Comment.MAX_LENGTH
    CommentCommand --> LogicManager : throws CommandException
    note right of CommentCommand
      Two comments that are each within the limit can exceed
      it once joined, which is why appending is checked again
      here. The student keeps their current comment and
      nothing below this point runs.
    end note
  end

  CommentCommand -> Existing : append(comment)
  activate Existing
  Existing --> CommentCommand : updatedComment
  deactivate Existing
end

CommentCommand -> Person : withComment(updatedComment)
activate Person
Person --> CommentCommand : updated
deactivate Person

note right of Person
  Person and Comment are immutable, so append and withComment
  return new objects rather than changing existing or p.
end note

CommentCommand -> Model : setPerson(p, updated)
activate Model
note right of Model
  The displayed list is not re-filtered, so the
  indexes the TA sees stay stable.
end note
Model --> CommentCommand
deactivate Model

CommentCommand --> LogicManager : r:CommandResult
deactivate CommentCommand

[<-- LogicManager : r
deactivate LogicManager
@enduml
